        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Now the model is gone. We learn value functions from *sampled experience* alone.\nTwo pure strategies sit at opposite ends of a spectrum, and the trade-off between\nthem — bias versus variance, set by how much you *bootstrap* — is one of the most\nimportant dials in all of RL."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#003",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|        THE SPECTRUM: HOW FAR DO YOU LOOK BEFORE UPDATING?        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  MONTE CARLO                  TD(lambda)            TD(0)        |\n|  (full return)                (n-step blend)        (one step)   |\n|  ----------                   -----------           -------      |\n|  wait for episode end         intermediate         bootstrap now |\n|  G_t = r + gr + g^2 r + ...   geometric mix         r + g V(s')  |\n|                                                                  |\n|  no bootstrap                 partial bootstrap   full bootstrap |\n|  UNBIASED                                           BIASED       |\n|  HIGH variance                                      LOW variance |\n|                                                                  |\n|  lambda = 1  <----------------------------------->  lambda = 0   |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#004",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read it left-to-right as the bootstrapping dial.** Pure Monte Carlo waits for\nthe true return (unbiased, high variance). TD(0) updates immediately toward its\nown estimate (biased by that estimate, low variance). TD(lambda) interpolates."
    },
