      "text": "## Monte Carlo Prediction"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#007",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Estimate `v_pi(s)` by *averaging actual returns* observed after visiting `s`. No\nmodel, no bootstrapping — just the law of large numbers."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#008",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  MONTE CARLO PREDICTION                                          |\n|                                                                  |\n|  run an episode under pi:  S0,A0,R1,S1,...,S_T  (terminal)       |\n|  for each state S_t visited, compute the realized return:        |\n|     G_t = R_{t+1} + gamma R_{t+2} + ... + gamma^{T-t-1} R_T      |\n|  update toward it:                                               |\n|     V(S_t)  <-  V(S_t) + alpha [ G_t - V(S_t) ]                  |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#009",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "`G_t` is an *unbiased* sample of `v_pi(S_t)` — its expectation is exactly the\nvalue. Averaging many such samples converges to the true value."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#010",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  first-visit MC:  average return after the FIRST visit to s per episode\n  every-visit MC:  average return after EVERY visit to s\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md#011",
      "path": [
        "03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td, git-history:reinforcement-learning:03-monte-carlo-and-td]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "concepts": "[monte carlo, temporal difference, TD(0), TD(lambda), eligibility traces, bias variance]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/03-MONTE-CARLO-AND-TD.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:monte-carlo-and-td",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[temporal difference]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Monte Carlo and Temporal Difference Learning",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Both converge; first-visit gives an unbiased mean of i.i.d. returns. The catch:\nMC needs *complete episodes* (no learning in continuing tasks) and the returns\nare high-variance because they accumulate randomness from the entire trajectory."
    },
